<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Extended Related Work</h2>

<section id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Disagreement in Human Judgments.</h4>

<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Psychology studies have shown that even when individuals are presented with the same evidence, they can rationally arrive at different choices for what is the “best” because of systematic differences in their judgmental processes <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib23" title="" class="ltx_ref">Mumpower and Stewart, 1996</a>)</cite>,
including (i) different problem definitions, where disagreement stems from judging different environmental criteria or a confusion between scientific facts and personal value, (ii) different organizing principles, where individuals may apply different cue weights, function forms, or overall biases when integrating the same set of information, as explained by Social Judgment Theory <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">Brehmer, 1976</a>)</cite>, and (iii) different mental models about how the evidence was generated.
In our context, this explains why human annotators can disagree about LLM outputs even under identical prompts or instructions: they face different value trade-offs (e.g., safety vs. helpfulness) or apply different thresholds for judgment, which may result in distinct yet internally coherent choices of what is preferred.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Probabilistic Models of Agreement.</h4>

<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Probabilistic modeling of agreement dates back to the 1950s.
Classic models such as the <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">Dawid and Skene (1979)</a></cite> model aim to infer a single “gold standard” label from multiple, often noisy, annotators.
Studies <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib27" title="" class="ltx_ref">Passonneau and Carpenter, 2014</a>; <a href="#bib.bib28" title="" class="ltx_ref">Paun et al., 2018</a>)</cite> have shown that by modeling annotator reliability, these methods can produce high-quality data even from non-expert crowd workers and outperform simpler aggregation techniques such as majority vote.
In contrast to this approach, a recent line of work shows that, for many complex and subjective tasks, disagreement is not simply noise but a valid and reproducible signal that reflects legitimate differences in human interpretation <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib29" title="" class="ltx_ref">Pavlick and Kwiatkowski, 2019</a>; <a href="#bib.bib25" title="" class="ltx_ref">Nie et al., 2020</a>)</cite>.
Our probabilistic autorater aligns with this view by treating the annotator heterogeneity as the prediction target to capture the full distribution of human judgments.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Learning from Human Feedback.</h4>

<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Canonical Reinforcement Learning from Human Feedback (RLHF) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib26" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ouyang et al., 2022</a>)</cite> involves learning a reward model from pairwise human preferences, often by fitting a Bradley-Terry model via maximum likelihood estimation.
This approach implicitly assumes that heterogeneous feedback from different humans is merely a noisy estimate of a single ground-truth preference.
However, a growing body of work <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib24" title="" class="ltx_ref">Munos et al., 2024</a>; <a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ge et al., 2024</a>; <a href="#bib.bib36" title="" class="ltx_ref">Siththaranjan et al., 2024</a>)</cite> suggests that, in the context of AI alignment, preference heterogeneity often reflects legitimate differences in individual values and should be modeled directly rather than averaged away.
Our research complements this line of work as our finetuned probabilistic autoraters can be employed in such preference-based RL to better align models with the diversity of human preferences.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Proofs</h2>

<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>Preference Distribution and Estimation</h3>

<div id="A2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math> index an annotator drawn from a population distribution <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(h)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(h)</annotation></semantics></math>. For a pairwise input <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{X}}={\bm{x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝑿</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{X}}={\bm{x}}</annotation></semantics></math>, define the annotator-specific preference probability</p>
<table id="A2.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p_{h}({\bm{x}})\;=\;\Pr[Y=1\mid{\bm{X}}={\bm{x}},h],\qquad Y\in\{0,1\}\ \text{($1$ indicates $B\succ A$)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝑿</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mtext>(</mtext><mn>1</mn><mtext> indicates </mtext><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>≻</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mtext>)</mtext></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{h}({\bm{x}})\;=\;\Pr[Y=1\mid{\bm{X}}={\bm{x}},h],\qquad Y\in\{0,1\}\ \text{($1$ indicates $B\succ A$)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The population (ground-truth) preference is the annotator-average:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{*}({\bm{x}})\;=\;\mathbb{E}_{h\sim p(h)}[\,p_{h}({\bm{x}})\,]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{*}({\bm{x}})\;=\;\mathbb{E}_{h\sim p(h)}[\,p_{h}({\bm{x}})\,].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">A common special case here is when annotators hold <em id="A2.SS1.p1.3.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">stable</em> preferences, i.e.,
where <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{h}({\bm{x}})\in\{0,1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{h}({\bm{x}})\in\{0,1\}</annotation></semantics></math> (each annotator has a fixed judgment per <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒙</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}</annotation></semantics></math>). In that case, <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{h}({\bm{x}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{h}({\bm{x}})</annotation></semantics></math> is the indicator of “<math id="A2.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math> prefers B” and <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{*}({\bm{x}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{*}({\bm{x}})</annotation></semantics></math> is the population fraction preferring B.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Given <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> i.i.d. labels <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{y^{(j)}\}_{j=1}^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{y^{(j)}\}_{j=1}^{m}</annotation></semantics></math> collected by sampling annotators <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{j}\stackrel{{\scriptstyle\text{i.i.d.}}}{{\sim}}p(h)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mover><mo>∼</mo><mtext>i.i.d.</mtext></mover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{j}\stackrel{{\scriptstyle\text{i.i.d.}}}{{\sim}}p(h)</annotation></semantics></math> and then <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y^{(j)}\sim\mathrm{Bernoulli}(p_{h_{j}}({\bm{x}}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>Bernoulli</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y^{(j)}\sim\mathrm{Bernoulli}(p_{h_{j}}({\bm{x}}))</annotation></semantics></math>, the Monte Carlo estimator</p>
<table id="A2.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{p}_{m}({\bm{x}})\;=\;\frac{1}{m}\sum_{j=1}^{m}y^{(j)}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>m</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{p}_{m}({\bm{x}})\;=\;\frac{1}{m}\sum_{j=1}^{m}y^{(j)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">is an unbiased estimate of <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{*}({\bm{x}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{*}({\bm{x}})</annotation></semantics></math> with variance decreasing as <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/m</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 2</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Unbiasedness and variance of the multi-annotator estimate)<span id="Thmtheorem2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For any fixed <math id="Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}</annotation></semantics></math> and i.i.d. sampling as above,</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\!\left[\hat{p}_{m}({\bm{x}})\right]\;=\;p^{*}({\bm{x}}),\qquad\mathrm{Var}\!\left[\hat{p}_{m}({\bm{x}})\right]\;=\;\frac{p^{*}({\bm{x}})\bigl(1-p^{*}({\bm{x}})\bigr)}{m}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.643em;" width="1.643em"><mi>Var</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\!\left[\hat{p}_{m}({\bm{x}})\right]\;=\;p^{*}({\bm{x}}),\qquad\mathrm{Var}\!\left[\hat{p}_{m}({\bm{x}})\right]\;=\;\frac{p^{*}({\bm{x}})\bigl(1-p^{*}({\bm{x}})\bigr)}{m}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">By the law of total expectation, <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[y^{(j)}\mid{\bm{x}}]=\mathbb{E}_{h}[p_{h}({\bm{x}})]=p^{*}({\bm{x}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[y^{(j)}\mid{\bm{x}}]=\mathbb{E}_{h}[p_{h}({\bm{x}})]=p^{*}({\bm{x}})</annotation></semantics></math>, so <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\hat{p}_{m}({\bm{x}})]=p^{*}({\bm{x}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\hat{p}_{m}({\bm{x}})]=p^{*}({\bm{x}})</annotation></semantics></math>. Since the <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y^{(j)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y^{(j)}</annotation></semantics></math> are i.i.d. Bernoulli with mean <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{*}({\bm{x}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{*}({\bm{x}})</annotation></semantics></math> (marginalizing over <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math>),
<math id="A2.SS1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Var}(\hat{p}_{m}({\bm{x}}))=\mathrm{Var}(y^{(1)})/m=p^{*}({\bm{x}})(1-p^{*}({\bm{x}}))/m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Var}(\hat{p}_{m}({\bm{x}}))=\mathrm{Var}(y^{(1)})/m=p^{*}({\bm{x}})(1-p^{*}({\bm{x}}))/m</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.2 </span>Proof of Proposition <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Proposition 1 (Fisher Consistency of Brier and Log Rewards). ‣ 3.1 Consistency Analysis ‣ 3 Finetuning Autoraters to Match the Preference Distribution ‣ Judging with Confidence: Calibrating Autoraters to Preference Distributions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a></h3>

<div id="A2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We first recall the setup. For <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\bm{X}},Y)\sim\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑿</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\bm{X}},Y)\sim\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y\in\{0,1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y\in\{0,1\}</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="A2.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y\mid{\bm{X}}={\bm{x}}\sim\mathrm{Bernoulli}(p^{*}({\bm{x}}))," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝑿</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>Bernoulli</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y\mid{\bm{X}}={\bm{x}}\sim\mathrm{Bernoulli}(p^{*}({\bm{x}})),</annotation></semantics></math>
the policy <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{\pi}}_{\bm{\theta}}({\bm{\tau}}\mid{\bm{x}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝝅</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝉</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{\pi}}_{\bm{\theta}}({\bm{\tau}}\mid{\bm{x}})</annotation></semantics></math> emits a token sequence <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{\tau}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝝉</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{\tau}}</annotation></semantics></math> intended to encode a numeric probability. A deterministic parser
<math id="A2.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g:\mathcal{T}\to[0,1]\cup\{\bot\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⊥</mo><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g:\mathcal{T}\to[0,1]\cup\{\bot\}</annotation></semantics></math>
returns either a number <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> or the unparsable symbol <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bot" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊥</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bot</annotation></semantics></math>. Let
<math id="A2.SS2.p1.m9" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="s_{\bm{\theta}}({\bm{x}})=\Pr_{{\bm{\tau}}\sim{\bm{\pi}}_{\bm{\theta}}(\cdot\mid{\bm{x}})}[g({\bm{\tau}})\neq\bot]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mi>𝝉</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>𝝅</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝉</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">≠</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⊥</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{\bm{\theta}}({\bm{x}})=\Pr_{{\bm{\tau}}\sim{\bm{\pi}}_{\bm{\theta}}(\cdot\mid{\bm{x}})}[g({\bm{\tau}})\neq\bot]</annotation></semantics></math>.
The piecewise rewards are:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex10" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex10X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex10X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle R_{\mathrm{Brier}}({\bm{\tau}};y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>Brier</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝉</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle R_{\mathrm{Brier}}({\bm{\tau}};y)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex10X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\begin{cases}1-(p-y)^{2},&amp;g({\bm{\tau}})=p\in[0,1],\\
0,&amp;g({\bm{\tau}})=\bot,\end{cases}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝉</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝉</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⊥</mo><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\begin{cases}1-(p-y)^{2},&amp;g({\bm{\tau}})=p\in[0,1],\\
0,&amp;g({\bm{\tau}})=\bot,\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex10Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex10Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle R_{\mathrm{Log}}({\bm{\tau}};y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>Log</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝉</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle R_{\mathrm{Log}}({\bm{\tau}};y)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex10Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\begin{cases}y\log p^{\prime}+(1-y)\log(1-p^{\prime}),&amp;g({\bm{\tau}})=p\in[0,1],\\
\log\epsilon,&amp;g({\bm{\tau}})=\bot,\end{cases}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝉</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝉</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⊥</mo><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\begin{cases}y\log p^{\prime}+(1-y)\log(1-p^{\prime}),&amp;g({\bm{\tau}})=p\in[0,1],\\
\log\epsilon,&amp;g({\bm{\tau}})=\bot,\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">with <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{\prime}=\mathrm{clip}(p,\epsilon,1-\epsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>clip</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{\prime}=\mathrm{clip}(p,\epsilon,1-\epsilon)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon\in(0,\tfrac{1}{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon\in(0,\tfrac{1}{2})</annotation></semantics></math>. The population objective is
<math id="A2.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="J_{R}({\bm{\theta}})=\mathbb{E}_{({\bm{X}},Y)}\,\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{\tau}}\sim{\bm{\pi}}_{\bm{\theta}}(\cdot\mid{\bm{X}})}[R({\bm{\tau}};Y)]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑿</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝝉</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>𝝅</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝑿</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝉</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J_{R}({\bm{\theta}})=\mathbb{E}_{({\bm{X}},Y)}\,\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{\tau}}\sim{\bm{\pi}}_{\bm{\theta}}(\cdot\mid{\bm{X}})}[R({\bm{\tau}};Y)].</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Fix <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒙</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}</annotation></semantics></math> and abbreviate <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{*}=p^{*}({\bm{x}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{*}=p^{*}({\bm{x}})</annotation></semantics></math>. All statements below are conditional on <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{X}}={\bm{x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝑿</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{X}}={\bm{x}}</annotation></semantics></math> and the conclusion holds for almost every <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒙</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}</annotation></semantics></math> (w.r.t. the marginal of <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑿</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{X}}</annotation></semantics></math>).</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">This proof utilizes the following observations:
(i) for any random variable <math id="A2.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math> with finite variance and any constant <math id="A2.SS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[(Z-a)^{2}]=(\mathbb{E}[Z]-a)^{2}+\mathrm{Var}(Z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[(Z-a)^{2}]=(\mathbb{E}[Z]-a)^{2}+\mathrm{Var}(Z)</annotation></semantics></math>;
(ii) the function <math id="A2.SS2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi(p)=p^{*}\log p+(1-p^{*})\log(1-p)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi(p)=p^{*}\log p+(1-p^{*})\log(1-p)</annotation></semantics></math> is strictly concave on <math id="A2.SS2.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\in(\epsilon,1-\epsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\in(\epsilon,1-\epsilon)</annotation></semantics></math> with unique maximizer at <math id="A2.SS2.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p=p^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p=p^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> (and at the boundary when <math id="A2.SS2.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{*}\notin(\epsilon,1-\epsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>∉</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{*}\notin(\epsilon,1-\epsilon)</annotation></semantics></math>).</p>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Brier.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> denote the random numeric report <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g({\bm{\tau}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝉</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g({\bm{\tau}})</annotation></semantics></math> conditional on <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="g({\bm{\tau}})\neq\bot" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝉</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">≠</mo><mo lspace="0em">⊥</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g({\bm{\tau}})\neq\bot</annotation></semantics></math> (so <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> is defined with probability <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{\bm{\theta}}({\bm{x}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{\bm{\theta}}({\bm{x}})</annotation></semantics></math>). Then</p>
<table id="A2.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{\tau}},Y}\!\left[R_{\mathrm{Brier}}({\bm{\tau}};Y)\mid{\bm{x}}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝝉</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>Brier</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝉</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{\tau}},Y}\!\left[R_{\mathrm{Brier}}({\bm{\tau}};Y)\mid{\bm{x}}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=s_{\bm{\theta}}({\bm{x}})\,\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{\tau}}}\!\left[\,\mathbb{E}_{Y\mid{\bm{x}}}\bigl[1-(P-Y)^{2}\bigr]\right]+\bigl(1-s_{\bm{\theta}}({\bm{x}})\bigr)\cdot 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>𝝉</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.170em">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=s_{\bm{\theta}}({\bm{x}})\,\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{\tau}}}\!\left[\,\mathbb{E}_{Y\mid{\bm{x}}}\bigl[1-(P-Y)^{2}\bigr]\right]+\bigl(1-s_{\bm{\theta}}({\bm{x}})\bigr)\cdot 0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright" colspan="3"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=s_{\bm{\theta}}({\bm{x}})\,\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{\tau}}}\!\left[1-\,\mathbb{E}_{Y\mid{\bm{x}}}\bigl[(Y-P)^{2}\bigr]\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>𝝉</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo rspace="0.392em">−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=s_{\bm{\theta}}({\bm{x}})\,\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{\tau}}}\!\left[1-\,\mathbb{E}_{Y\mid{\bm{x}}}\bigl[(Y-P)^{2}\bigr]\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright" colspan="3"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=s_{\bm{\theta}}({\bm{x}})\,\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{\tau}}}\!\left[1-\,\left(\mathbb{E}_{Y\mid{\bm{x}}}[Y]-P\right)^{2}-\mathrm{Var}_{Y\mid{\bm{x}}}(Y)\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>𝝉</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo rspace="0.392em">−</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo rspace="0.392em">−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Var</mi><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=s_{\bm{\theta}}({\bm{x}})\,\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{\tau}}}\!\left[1-\,\left(\mathbb{E}_{Y\mid{\bm{x}}}[Y]-P\right)^{2}-\mathrm{Var}_{Y\mid{\bm{x}}}(Y)\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="A2.Ex13.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">applying (i)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=s_{\bm{\theta}}({\bm{x}})\,\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{\tau}}}\!\left[1-\,\left(p^{*}-P\right)^{2}-p^{*}(1-p^{*})\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>𝝉</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo rspace="0.392em">−</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo rspace="0.392em">−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=s_{\bm{\theta}}({\bm{x}})\,\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{\tau}}}\!\left[1-\,\left(p^{*}-P\right)^{2}-p^{*}(1-p^{*})\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright" colspan="3"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=s_{\bm{\theta}}({\bm{x}})\,\Bigl(1-\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{\tau}}}\!\left[(P-p^{*})^{2}\right]-p^{*}(1-p^{*})\Bigr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>𝝉</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=s_{\bm{\theta}}({\bm{x}})\,\Bigl(1-\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{\tau}}}\!\left[(P-p^{*})^{2}\right]-p^{*}(1-p^{*})\Bigr)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright" colspan="3"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=s_{\bm{\theta}}({\bm{x}})\,\Bigl(1-\bigl[(\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{\tau}}}[P]-p^{*})^{2}+\mathrm{Var}_{{\bm{\tau}}}(P)\bigr]-p^{*}(1-p^{*})\Bigr)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>𝝉</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Var</mi><mi>𝝉</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=s_{\bm{\theta}}({\bm{x}})\,\Bigl(1-\bigl[(\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{\tau}}}[P]-p^{*})^{2}+\mathrm{Var}_{{\bm{\tau}}}(P)\bigr]-p^{*}(1-p^{*})\Bigr).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="A2.Ex16.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">applying (i)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">For fixed <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{\bm{\theta}}({\bm{x}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{\bm{\theta}}({\bm{x}})</annotation></semantics></math> this is maximized by setting <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Var}(P)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Var}(P)=0</annotation></semantics></math> (deterministic numeric output) and <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[P]=p^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[P]=p^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> (truthful reporting). Moreover, since
<math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-p^{*}(1-p^{*})&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-p^{*}(1-p^{*})&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, the expectation is positive when <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Var}(P)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Var}(P)=0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[P]=p^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[P]=p^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>. Increasing <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{\bm{\theta}}({\bm{x}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{\bm{\theta}}({\bm{x}})</annotation></semantics></math> strictly increases the expectation; hence an optimizer satisfies <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{\bm{\theta}}({\bm{x}})=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{\bm{\theta}}({\bm{x}})=1</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, at any global maximizer,
<math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> is almost surely constant and equals <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e., <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\bm{\theta}}({\bm{x}})=p^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\bm{\theta}}({\bm{x}})=p^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Log with clipping.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Write <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> for the clipped numeric report when parsable. Then</p>
<table id="A2.Ex17" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex17X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex17X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{\tau}},Y}\!\left[R_{\mathrm{Log}}({\bm{\tau}};Y)\mid{\bm{x}}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝝉</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>Log</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝉</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{\tau}},Y}\!\left[R_{\mathrm{Log}}({\bm{\tau}};Y)\mid{\bm{x}}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex17X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=s_{\bm{\theta}}({\bm{x}})\,\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{\tau}}}\!\left[\,\mathbb{E}_{Y|{\bm{x}}}\left[Y\log P^{\prime}+(1-Y)\log(1-P^{\prime})\right]\,\right]+(1-s_{\bm{\theta}}({\bm{x}}))\,\log\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>𝝉</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.170em">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.170em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=s_{\bm{\theta}}({\bm{x}})\,\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{\tau}}}\!\left[\,\mathbb{E}_{Y|{\bm{x}}}\left[Y\log P^{\prime}+(1-Y)\log(1-P^{\prime})\right]\,\right]+(1-s_{\bm{\theta}}({\bm{x}}))\,\log\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex17Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex17Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=s_{\bm{\theta}}({\bm{x}})\,\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{\tau}}}\!\left[\,p^{*}\log P^{\prime}+(1-p^{*})\log(1-P^{\prime})\,\right]+(1-s_{\bm{\theta}}({\bm{x}}))\,\log\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>𝝉</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.170em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=s_{\bm{\theta}}({\bm{x}})\,\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{\tau}}}\!\left[\,p^{*}\log P^{\prime}+(1-p^{*})\log(1-P^{\prime})\,\right]+(1-s_{\bm{\theta}}({\bm{x}}))\,\log\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex17Xb"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex17Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=s_{\bm{\theta}}({\bm{x}})\,\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{\tau}}}[\phi(P^{\prime})]+(1-s_{\bm{\theta}}({\bm{x}}))\log\epsilon." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>𝝉</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=s_{\bm{\theta}}({\bm{x}})\,\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{\tau}}}[\phi(P^{\prime})]+(1-s_{\bm{\theta}}({\bm{x}}))\log\epsilon.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">By strict concavity of <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math> and Jensen’s inequality,
<math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\phi(P^{\prime})]\leq\phi(\mathbb{E}[P^{\prime}])" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\phi(P^{\prime})]\leq\phi(\mathbb{E}[P^{\prime}])</annotation></semantics></math>
with equality iff <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> is almost surely constant (deterministic numeric output). The maximizer over <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P^{\prime}\in[\epsilon,1-\epsilon]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P^{\prime}\in[\epsilon,1-\epsilon]</annotation></semantics></math> is uniquely
<math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P^{\prime}\equiv\mathrm{clip}(p^{*},\epsilon,1-\epsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≡</mo><mrow><mi>clip</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P^{\prime}\equiv\mathrm{clip}(p^{*},\epsilon,1-\epsilon)</annotation></semantics></math>
(truthful reporting).
Finally, at this maximizer
<math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi\!\bigl(\mathrm{clip}(p^{*},\epsilon,1-\epsilon)\bigr)&gt;\log\epsilon," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.426em;" width="0.426em"><mi>ϕ</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>clip</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi\!\bigl(\mathrm{clip}(p^{*},\epsilon,1-\epsilon)\bigr)&gt;\log\epsilon,</annotation></semantics></math>
so allocating any mass to unparsable outputs (which yields <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>) strictly reduces the expectation; hence <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{\bm{\theta}}({\bm{x}})=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{\bm{\theta}}({\bm{x}})=1</annotation></semantics></math>.
Therefore, the optimal report is deterministic and equals the clipped truth <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{clip}(p^{*},\epsilon,1-\epsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>clip</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{clip}(p^{*},\epsilon,1-\epsilon)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Combining the two cases completes the proof.  <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\square" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">□</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\square</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Implementation Details</h2>

<section id="A3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.1 </span>Evaluation Details</h3>

<div id="A3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We measure the probabilistic autorater’s performance by comparing its judgment to human annotation or discretized probabilistic labels annotated by Gemini-2.5-Flash.
Following prior work <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib45" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wang et al., 2024b</a>; <a href="#bib.bib57" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhu et al., 2025</a>)</cite>, we formulate the pairwise judgment task as a three-class classification problem with labels <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A\succ B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>≻</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A\succ B</annotation></semantics></math>, Tie, and <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B\succ A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>≻</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B\succ A</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="TP_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">TP_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="FP_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">FP_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="FN_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">FN_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the true positives, false positives, and false negatives for class <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively. We report macro-averaged metrics by computing each score per class and then averaging over all <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> classes:</p>
<table id="A3.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{Precision}_{\text{macro}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext>Precision</mtext><mtext>macro</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{Precision}_{\text{macro}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex18.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{C}\sum_{i=1}^{C}\frac{TP_{i}}{TP_{i}+FP_{i}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>C</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>C</mi></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{C}\sum_{i=1}^{C}\frac{TP_{i}}{TP_{i}+FP_{i}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{Recall}_{\text{macro}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext>Recall</mtext><mtext>macro</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{Recall}_{\text{macro}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex19.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{C}\sum_{i=1}^{C}\frac{TP_{i}}{TP_{i}+FN_{i}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>C</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>C</mi></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{C}\sum_{i=1}^{C}\frac{TP_{i}}{TP_{i}+FN_{i}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{F1-score}_{\text{macro}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext>F1-score</mtext><mtext>macro</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{F1-score}_{\text{macro}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex20.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{C}\sum_{i=1}^{C}\frac{2\cdot TP_{i}}{2\cdot TP_{i}+FP_{i}+FN_{i}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>C</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>C</mi></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{C}\sum_{i=1}^{C}\frac{2\cdot TP_{i}}{2\cdot TP_{i}+FP_{i}+FN_{i}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="A3.Ex21.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">Agreement</span></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex21.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\sum_{i=1}^{C}TP_{i}}{\sum_{i=1}^{C}(TP_{i}+FN_{i})}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>C</mi></msubsup><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>C</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\sum_{i=1}^{C}TP_{i}}{\sum_{i=1}^{C}(TP_{i}+FN_{i})}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">By convention, calibration is measured with respect to a set of discrete (binary) labels.
To evaluate model calibration, we first binarize the preference distribution to obtain ground truth preference labels and then measure the Expected Calibration Error (ECE) and Brier Score.
Test samples with ground truth label being “Tie” are skipped for calibration evaluation.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The ECE is calculated by dividing the confidence into <math id="A3.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> equal-sized bins (each of size <math id="A3.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tfrac{1}{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>K</mi></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tfrac{1}{K}</annotation></semantics></math>), and then calculating the accuracy and average confidence within each bin:</p>
<table id="A3.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{ECE}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ECE</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{ECE}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex22.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{k=1}^{K}\frac{|B_{k}|}{N}\,\bigl|\mathrm{Acc}(B_{k})-\mathrm{Conf}(B_{k})\bigr|," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Acc</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>Conf</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{k=1}^{K}\frac{|B_{k}|}{N}\,\bigl|\mathrm{Acc}(B_{k})-\mathrm{Conf}(B_{k})\bigr|,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{Acc}(B_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Acc</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{Acc}(B_{k})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex23.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{|B_{k}|}\sum_{i\in B_{k}}\mathbf{1}\!\left(\hat{y}_{i}=y_{i}\right),\qquad\mathrm{Conf}(B_{k})=\frac{1}{|B_{k}|}\sum_{i\in B_{k}}\hat{p}_{i}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Conf</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{|B_{k}|}\sum_{i\in B_{k}}\mathbf{1}\!\left(\hat{y}_{i}=y_{i}\right),\qquad\mathrm{Conf}(B_{k})=\frac{1}{|B_{k}|}\sum_{i\in B_{k}}\hat{p}_{i},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A3.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> is the number of samples whose prediction confidence falls into the interval <math id="A3.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\tfrac{k-1}{K},\tfrac{k}{K}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mi>k</mi><mi>K</mi></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\tfrac{k-1}{K},\tfrac{k}{K}]</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.SS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{y}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{y}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> are the predicted and true preference labels, and <math id="A3.SS1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{p}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{p}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is the predicted probability.
By default, we set <math id="A3.SS1.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=10</annotation></semantics></math> in our experiments.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">The Brier score is calculated as <math id="A3.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tfrac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}(y_{i}-\hat{p}_{i})^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tfrac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}(y_{i}-\hat{p}_{i})^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.2 </span>Finetuning Details</h3>

<div id="A3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In Setting 2, we optimize the following GRPO objective <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib34" title="" class="ltx_ref">Shao et al., 2024</a>)</cite></p>
<table id="A3.Ex24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{J}({\bm{\theta}})=\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{x}}\sim p({\bm{x}}),{\bm{\tau}}\sim{\bm{\pi}}_{{\bm{\theta}}_{\mathrm{old}}}}\!\left[\min\!\left(\frac{{\bm{\pi}}_{\bm{\theta}}({\bm{\tau}}|{\bm{x}})}{{\bm{\pi}}_{{\bm{\theta}}_{\mathrm{old}}}({\bm{\tau}}|{\bm{x}})}\,A_{t},\;\operatorname{clip}\!\left(\frac{{\bm{\pi}}_{\bm{\theta}}({\bm{\tau}}|{\bm{x}})}{{\bm{\pi}}_{{\bm{\theta}}_{\mathrm{old}}}({\bm{\tau}}|{\bm{x}})},\,1-\varepsilon,\,1+\varepsilon\right)A_{t}\right)-\beta\,D_{\mathrm{KL}}\!\left({\bm{\pi}}_{\bm{\theta}}\,\|\,{\bm{\pi}}_{\mathrm{ref}}\right)\right]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>𝝉</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>𝝅</mi><msub><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>old</mi></msub></msub></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mpadded style="width:1.653em;" width="1.653em"><mi>min</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>𝝅</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝉</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝝅</mi><msub><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>old</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝉</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mpadded style="width:1.428em;" width="1.428em"><mi>clip</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>𝝅</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝉</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝝅</mi><msub><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>old</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝉</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mn> 1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo>,</mo><mn> 1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>𝝅</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.337em">∥</mo><msub><mi>𝝅</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{J}({\bm{\theta}})=\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{x}}\sim p({\bm{x}}),{\bm{\tau}}\sim{\bm{\pi}}_{{\bm{\theta}}_{\mathrm{old}}}}\!\left[\min\!\left(\frac{{\bm{\pi}}_{\bm{\theta}}({\bm{\tau}}|{\bm{x}})}{{\bm{\pi}}_{{\bm{\theta}}_{\mathrm{old}}}({\bm{\tau}}|{\bm{x}})}\,A_{t},\;\operatorname{clip}\!\left(\frac{{\bm{\pi}}_{\bm{\theta}}({\bm{\tau}}|{\bm{x}})}{{\bm{\pi}}_{{\bm{\theta}}_{\mathrm{old}}}({\bm{\tau}}|{\bm{x}})},\,1-\varepsilon,\,1+\varepsilon\right)A_{t}\right)-\beta\,D_{\mathrm{KL}}\!\left({\bm{\pi}}_{\bm{\theta}}\,\|\,{\bm{\pi}}_{\mathrm{ref}}\right)\right],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">with the unbiased KL estimator <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib33" title="" class="ltx_ref">Schulman, 2020</a>)</cite></p>
<table id="A3.Ex25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="D_{\mathrm{KL}}\!\left({\bm{\pi}}_{\bm{\theta}}\,\|\,{\bm{\pi}}_{\mathrm{ref}}\right)\approx\frac{{\bm{\pi}}_{\mathrm{ref}}({\bm{\tau}}|{\bm{x}})}{{\bm{\pi}}_{\bm{\theta}}({\bm{\tau}}|{\bm{x}})}-\log\!\frac{{\bm{\pi}}_{\mathrm{ref}}({\bm{\tau}}|{\bm{x}})}{{\bm{\pi}}_{\bm{\theta}}({\bm{\tau}}|{\bm{x}})}-1," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>𝝅</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.337em">∥</mo><msub><mi>𝝅</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>𝝅</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝉</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝝅</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝉</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mi>log</mi><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>𝝅</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝉</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝝅</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝉</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\mathrm{KL}}\!\left({\bm{\pi}}_{\bm{\theta}}\,\|\,{\bm{\pi}}_{\mathrm{ref}}\right)\approx\frac{{\bm{\pi}}_{\mathrm{ref}}({\bm{\tau}}|{\bm{x}})}{{\bm{\pi}}_{\bm{\theta}}({\bm{\tau}}|{\bm{x}})}-\log\!\frac{{\bm{\pi}}_{\mathrm{ref}}({\bm{\tau}}|{\bm{x}})}{{\bm{\pi}}_{\bm{\theta}}({\bm{\tau}}|{\bm{x}})}-1,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A3.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{\pi}}_{\bm{\theta}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝝅</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{\pi}}_{\bm{\theta}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the policy model being optimized,
<math id="A3.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{\pi}}_{{\bm{\theta}}_{\mathrm{old}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝝅</mi><msub><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>old</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{\pi}}_{{\bm{\theta}}_{\mathrm{old}}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the previous policy model,
<math id="A3.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{\pi}}_{\mathrm{ref}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝝅</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{\pi}}_{\mathrm{ref}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the reference policy,
<math id="A3.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is the advantage estimate,
<math id="A3.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math> is the clipping hyperparameter,
and <math id="A3.SS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> is the KL penalty coefficient.
Detailed parameter settings for our experiments are presented in Table <a href="#A3.T5" title="Table 5 ‣ C.2 Finetuning Details ‣ Appendix C Implementation Details ‣ Judging with Confidence: Calibrating Autoraters to Preference Distributions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>.</p>
</div>
