<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Additional Results</h2>

<section id="A4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.1 </span>Win Rate Prediction</h3>

<div id="A4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We use a subset of the LMSys Chatbot Arena Conversation dataset <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib54" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zheng et al., 2023</a>; <a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kahng et al., 2025</a>)</cite> to evaluate the autorater’s ability to predict the LM’s win rate.
This subset contains a total of 900 prompts for comparing responses from Gemma 1.0 and Gemma 1.1.
For this evaluation, we use Qwen-2.5-7B as the base model for the autorater to avoid potential self-enhancement bias (i.e., favoring responses generated by LMs from the same family).
Specifically, given two LMs <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{\pi}}_{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝝅</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{\pi}}_{A}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{\pi}}_{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝝅</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{\pi}}_{B}</annotation></semantics></math>, the win rate (of <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{\pi}}_{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝝅</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{\pi}}_{B}</annotation></semantics></math>) is defined as</p>
<table id="A4.Ex26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Pr[{\bm{\pi}}_{B}\succ{\bm{\pi}}_{A}]\coloneqq\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{x}}\sim p({\bm{x}})}\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{\tau}}_{A}\sim{\bm{\pi}}_{A},{\bm{\tau}}_{B}\sim{\bm{\pi}}_{B}}\Pr[{\bm{\tau}}_{B}\succ{\bm{\tau}}_{A}|{\bm{x}}]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>𝝅</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo>≻</mo><msub><mi>𝝅</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>≔</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝝉</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>𝝅</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝝉</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>𝝅</mi><mi>B</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msub><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>𝝉</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo>≻</mo><msub><mi>𝝉</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr[{\bm{\pi}}_{B}\succ{\bm{\pi}}_{A}]\coloneqq\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{x}}\sim p({\bm{x}})}\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{\tau}}_{A}\sim{\bm{\pi}}_{A},{\bm{\tau}}_{B}\sim{\bm{\pi}}_{B}}\Pr[{\bm{\tau}}_{B}\succ{\bm{\tau}}_{A}|{\bm{x}}].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">From the results shown in Table <a href="#A4.T6" title="Table 6 ‣ D.1 Win Rate Prediction ‣ Appendix D Additional Results ‣ Judging with Confidence: Calibrating Autoraters to Preference Distributions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>, we observe that the predicted win rates from the finetuned autoraters are more aligned with the true win rate voted by human judges.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A4.T6" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 6: </span>Evaluation on the Chatbot Arena Conversations dataset for comparing Gemma 1.0 to Gemma 1.1. We compare the autorater’s predicted win rate for Gemma 1.0 against the true win rate from human annotators.
</figcaption>
